        "If any intermediate stage throws an exception, all subsequent standard stages (`thenApply`, `thenAccept`, `thenCompose`) are bypassed and complete exceptionally. Downstream stages are only executed if an intervening recovery stage (`exceptionally()` or `handle()`) catches the exception and returns a valid replacement value."
